The engine session every bot speaks follows the htttx bot protocol; the
contract mirrors its schemas' field names and bounds, and the Bot API copies
its schema block verbatim. It is published under the MIT License.
htttx-bot-api
https://github.com/hex-tic-tac-toe/htttx-bot-api
Copyright (c) 2026 hex-tic-tac-toe

The rating system is Glicko-2, the published method of Mark Glickman.
https://www.glicko.net/glicko/glicko2.pdf

How the site works, the rating settings, and the name rule take ideas and
parameter values from lichess; no code is copied from it.
https://lichess.org

